# TODO - Tahoe ABI

## Objective

Research public Tahoe KDK/SDK exports, IOPCIFamily, IO80211FamilyLegacy,
IOSkywalkFamily and IONetworkingFamily. Document method/lifetime contracts and
source-level compatibility, with explicit unverified assumptions and
fail-closed behavior. **No live logs needed.**

## Acceptance

- [ ] Implement/review the stated source and integrate on main.
- [ ] Account for exported symbols, ABI uncertainty and fail-closed interfaces.
- [ ] Ground decisions in public code, published standards and SDK/KDK references.
- [ ] Record unresolved assumptions and fail-closed behavior.
- [ ] Complete with source/static evidence, NEVER requiring a physical Dell test.

## Required source deliverables

- [ ] Pin Intel Darwin 25 / Tahoe 26.7.2 build 25G332 evidence and distinguish
      full symbol tables, actual exports and kernel/KPI eligibility.
- [ ] Specify every imported PCI/DMA/native-Wi-Fi method's signature,
      superclass layout, required virtual slots and object/buffer lifetime.
      Symbol-name presence alone does not establish a callable ABI.
- [ ] Compare the intended SDK declarations with the exact KDK evidence;
      document each discrepancy and its implemented resolution. Keep a
      required native path open if its ABI remains unknown/unimplementable.
- [ ] Identify all proposed target imports/dependencies in source and the
      Xcode target. Resolve source-known unsupported imports; actual binary
      relocation inspection belongs to the separately authorized build.

## Start here and next implementation step

Use docs/design/TAHOE-25G332-KDK.md, the exact-build symbol report and
TAHOE-25G332-KERNEL-DMA-TYPES.json under docs/evidence/. The latter covers
kernel/IOKit types; it does not establish IO80211 object layouts or exports.
Check actual PBXSourcesBuildPhase membership and conditional macros before
attributing imports to the active kext. Navigator entries alone are not built.

Produce one actionable API table: caller/source, image/build/UUID, signature,
export/KPI evidence, required virtual layout and ownership contract. Resolve
PCI and wireless families separately. Choose a target-provided native Wi-Fi
family before defining controller/interface subclasses; do not silently
substitute restored IO80211FamilyLegacy components for the exact Tahoe image.
A missing private ABI fact remains a concrete source blocker to investigate.

Primary references: [IOPCIFamily source](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/IOPCIFamily),
[IODMACommand source](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/blob/main/iokit/Kernel/IODMACommand.cpp),
and the versioned SDK/KDK evidence already retained in this repository.

## El Capitan reverse-engineering decision

Do not add a whole-driver El Capitan decompilation project to the critical
path. ath9k explicitly names AR9565/0036; OCLP's AirPortAtheros40 inventory
lists 0030 and older devices, not 0036. That inventory is not a complete
silicon-support proof, and a 0030 spoof proves no AR9565 compatibility.
[ath9k identity definitions](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/hw.h),
[OCLP device inventory](https://github.com/dortania/OpenCore-Legacy-Patcher/blob/main/opencore_legacy_patcher/datasets/pci_data.py).

Use Ghidra/static disassembly only for a specific unanswered ABI/lifetime
question, prioritizing the exact 25G332 binary. State the question and the
observation needed to answer it; do not treat decompiled pseudocode as original,
complete source or mix it into the new driver. If needed, put curated findings
in reference/ and scratch binaries/projects/output in .temp/reference/.
No bulk reconstruction, copied legacy stack or additional archive is required.

## Evidence

- Source commits, reference URLs/version/rights, static review and lint diagnostics.
- Theoretical completeness only; no kext build, device scan, packet logs or hardware claims.
- Add offline host tests only where material behavior/error paths warrant them;
  run through tools/validate.py --tests without treating them as hardware proof.
